    "text": "To determine how much Mr. McPherson needs to raise to complete the rent, we start by calculating how much Mrs. McPherson will raise. The rent is $1200 per year, and Mrs. McPherson will raise 30% of this amount.\n\nFirst, we calculate 30% of $1200:\n\\[\n0.30 \\times 1200 = 360\n\\]\nSo, Mrs. McPherson will raise $360. This means that the total amount needed to be raised is $1200, and Mrs. McPherson will raise $360 of it. Therefore, the amount Mr. McPherson needs to raise is:\n\\[\n1200 - 360 = 840\n\\]\nThus, Mr. McPherson needs to raise \\(\\boxed{840}\\) dollars to complete the rent.",
